{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMki8SXaV4Vcaz25x8S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the Intervals.icu connection; it had three separate causes, and the details are in `ANSWER.md`. I tested the whole flow against a fake Intervals server I ran locally, not the real one. So the app's side is checked, but my reading of how Intervals behaves isn't.\n\n1. **The Connect button returned 401 for everyone.** It was a plain link, and clicking a link loads a new page, which doesn't send the sign-in token the app keeps in the browser. The start-connection endpoint is now an authenticated POST that returns the Intervals URL, and the button calls it and then opens that URL. This matches the log exactly.\n2. **Intervals answered the authorize step with `invalid_request`.** The permissions string named the same area twice (`ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE` and `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`), and asking for write access already includes read. It's now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. This one is an inference: our log shows a bare `invalid_request`, not the `Duplicate scope` message in the note. It fits the evidence: the request broke when calendar access was added, Rivera's grant that worked named each area once, and removing the other parameters gave the same error. The first real connection will confirm it.\n3. **Rivera was told to reconnect after an hour.** Intervals tokens don't expire, but the code assumed they last one hour, then marked the connection expired and deleted a token that still worked. Now there's no expiry unless Intervals gives one. If Intervals ever rejects the token, the app clears it and shows \"revoked, reconnect\" instead of an error.\n\nI also added a check so a reconnect can't silently link a different Intervals account; the athlete has to disconnect first.\n\nOn the fake server: the old GET endpoint now returns 404, the connection completes, wellness data comes back, and after a simulated revoke the card shows the reconnect prompt.\n\n**What you need to do in prod:** athletes whose connection was already marked expired have lost their token, so Rivera and anyone like them will need to click Connect once more. That works now.\n\nFrom the colleague's note, I used:\n- the POST start endpoint\n- the each-area-once permissions rule\n- the \"tokens never expire, handle revocation on the first rejection\" approach\n- the account-mismatch check\n\nI didn't use:\n- **The simpler token exchange:** ours sends two extra fields, but Rivera's exchange succeeded with them and nothing in the logs points at it.\n- **The JWT `state`:** the existing signed state already carries the user and a 15-minute limit.\n- **Encrypting tokens at rest:** this repo keeps everything in memory, but it's worth doing on the prod table since the tokens never expire.\n- **The steps that need a real Intervals account:** those are outside the ground rules.\n\nNothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2315,"cache_read_input_tokens":35517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2315},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4507bebf-7542-4adc-bcb7-11ba9c95c40b","uuid":"f88dcf33-5e54-4ee4-8eff-19bdb93e2c94","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:29:56.615Z","request_id":"req_011CgEMkhkdBNfjTxf1zkxFP"}
